Occupied-armor unequip is the only policy change. Tools stay first and unchanged (`candidate.nim:551-570`). Helm/chest/legs then fill empty slots as before (`576-577`). Occupied slots unequip only for a key-addressable **strictly** higher tier (`578-581`); equal/lower never remove; a missing equipped key skips that kind (`582`).

Issuance and confirmation are separate. `act` stores the wire tick, confirms pending from the fresh observation, then records issuance from the selected action (`897-916`, `990-1001`). `armorUnequipIntent` requires not in combat, an equipped armor key, matching equipment scalar, and a strictly better replacement (`623-650`). Confirmation needs a later same-slot armor item with `freshTier > oldTier`; empty and unchanged scalars do not confirm (`652-667`). Pending is one record per armor slot and is cleared on life reset (`324-348`); counters persist.

